9

Protection orders available to the Court – The Court may, in issuing a protection order under section 5, 6 or 7 prohibit the respondent from:
(a)	committing any act of domestic violence or enlisting the help of another person to commit such act;
(b)	entering a residence, or part of such residence, shared by the complainant and the respondent;
(c)	entering the complainant’s place of employment, or
part of such place;

(d)	preventing the complainant who ordinarily lives or lived in a shared residence from entering or remaining in the shared residence; or
(e)	committing any other act, which the Court considers appropriate in the circumstances, in order to protect the complainant.

